Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [clang version workaround]

Clang 20.1 crashes (SIGSEGV in Sema::SetDeclDefaulted) when compiling
a defaulted operator== for OriginWithPossibleWildcards which contains
a mojom::CSPSource member. Work around the ICE by spelling out the
comparison explicitly instead of using = default.

Signed-off-by: avocado <avocado@avocadolinux.com>

--- a/services/network/public/cpp/permissions_policy/origin_with_possible_wildcards.cc
+++ b/services/network/public/cpp/permissions_policy/origin_with_possible_wildcards.cc
@@ -93,8 +93,10 @@ bool OriginWithPossibleWildcards::DoesMatchOrigin(
                                  network::CSPSourceContext::PermissionsPolicy);
 }

-bool operator==(const OriginWithPossibleWildcards& lhs,
-                const OriginWithPossibleWildcards& rhs) = default;
+bool operator==(const OriginWithPossibleWildcards& lhs,
+                const OriginWithPossibleWildcards& rhs) {
+  return !(lhs.csp_source < rhs.csp_source) && !(rhs.csp_source < lhs.csp_source);
+}

 std::strong_ordering operator<=>(const OriginWithPossibleWildcards& lhs,
                                  const OriginWithPossibleWildcards& rhs) {
